{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466398",
      "title": "Transforming Response Data",
      "lectureOrder": 608,
      "videoOrder": 560,
      "sourceHash": "0f3bc5f7731e4f9276e65833885c9a31d1d88efd7a1ffafd1373ffde8d11ba31",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 3.173,
          "en": "Instructor: We're almost done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.173,
          "end": 6.48,
          "en": "but there is some cleanup work we can do related to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.48,
          "end": 9.75,
          "en": "It's nice that we can unload and store our recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.75,
          "end": 11.97,
          "en": "That first of all means that we no longer need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.97,
          "end": 14.04,
          "en": "our default recipes here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.04,
          "end": 17.04,
          "en": "So I will comment that out just to have it around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.04,
          "end": 18.78,
          "en": "in case we do need it again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.78,
          "end": 20.82,
          "en": "or we want that dummy data again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.82,
          "end": 23.73,
          "en": "But I will initialize the recipes property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.73,
          "end": 25.95,
          "en": "which is an array of recipes just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.95,
          "end": 27.24,
          "en": "as an MT array now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.24,
          "end": 28.59,
          "en": "So that when our app loads,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 28.59,
          "end": 30.87,
          "en": "we have no recipes and we need to load them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 30.87,
          "end": 31.95,
          "en": "That, of course, is optional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 31.95,
          "end": 33.3,
          "en": "but I guess it makes a bit more sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 33.3,
          "end": 34.95,
          "en": "than loading some dummy data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 34.95,
          "end": 37.9,
          "en": "Obviously, you could do the same in the shopping list area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 38.94,
          "end": 40.59,
          "en": "Now that's the first change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 40.59,
          "end": 43.11,
          "en": "And we also have a bug in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 43.11,
          "end": 44.43,
          "en": "which we should fix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 44.43,
          "end": 49.43,
          "en": "Let's say we add a new recipe here, Summer Salad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 51.48,
          "end": 55.68,
          "en": "Add this image here, a juicy summer salad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.68,
          "end": 57,
          "en": "And now the important thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 57,
          "end": 59.31,
          "en": "I won't add any ingredients to that recipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 59.31,
          "end": 61.41,
          "en": "Instead, let's save it like this, which is valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 61.41,
          "end": 63.66,
          "en": "We don't need to have recipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 63.66,
          "end": 66.21,
          "en": "we don't need to have ingredients.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 66.21,
          "end": 68.31,
          "en": "And now let me store that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 68.31,
          "end": 69.9,
          "en": "So click save data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 69.9,
          "end": 73.32,
          "en": "and on fire base you can see there is a new item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 73.32,
          "end": 74.76,
          "en": "and that's our summer salad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 74.76,
          "end": 77.553,
          "en": "But please note, obviously it has no ingredients.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 78.42,
          "end": 81.72,
          "en": "Now, generally our app works here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 81.72,
          "end": 85.68,
          "en": "but to prevent nasty bugs when we're fetching the recipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 85.68,
          "end": 88.26,
          "en": "it would make sense that we make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 88.26,
          "end": 90.36,
          "en": "that we always have ingredients,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 90.36,
          "end": 92.1,
          "en": "even if it's just an MT array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 92.1,
          "end": 95.00999999999999,
          "en": "but that the data we loaded in the end has some ingredients",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 95.00999999999999,
          "end": 97.59,
          "en": "and this property is not undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 97.59,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "Because if we otherwise try to directly interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 103.5,
          "en": "with the ingredients, we could get errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 103.5,
          "end": 106.17,
          "en": "And for that, we can simply add pipe here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 106.17,
          "end": 109.533,
          "en": "to our fetch recipes, HTP request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 110.47,
          "end": 111.93,
          "en": "and add the map operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 111.93,
          "end": 114.423,
          "en": "which allows us to transform that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 115.68,
          "end": 120.68,
          "en": "For that, we just need to import map from rxjs operators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 126.78,
          "en": "And this, as you learned, is an observable operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.78,
          "end": 129.03,
          "en": "that allows you to transform the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 129.03,
          "end": 130.38,
          "en": "in an observable chain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.38,
          "end": 132.36,
          "en": "So right before subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 132.36,
          "end": 134.13,
          "en": "Here we get our recipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 134.13,
          "end": 138.256,
          "en": "but the recipes that might not have an ingredients property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 138.256,
          "end": 141.87,
          "en": "and now here we can simply return recipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 143.49,
          "en": "but call map on these two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 143.49,
          "end": 145.07999999999998,
          "en": "And now this can be confusing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 145.07999999999998,
          "end": 149.91,
          "en": "Map here in pipe is an rxjs operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 152.61,
          "en": "map here is called on an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 152.61,
          "end": 155.7,
          "en": "and therefore the normal JavaScript array method map,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 155.7,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "they happen to have the same name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 158.76,
          "en": "but they are not the same function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 158.76,
          "end": 161.79,
          "en": "That's an rxjs operator called as a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 161.79,
          "end": 163.29,
          "en": "like this inside of pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 163.29,
          "end": 165.78,
          "en": "That is a JavaScript array method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 165.78,
          "end": 167.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now map simply allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 167.57999999999998,
          "end": 169.74,
          "en": "to transform the elements in an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 169.74,
          "end": 171.54,
          "en": "In this case, in the recipes array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 171.54,
          "end": 172.86,
          "en": "It takes an anonymous function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 172.86,
          "end": 175.8,
          "en": "which is executed for every element in that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 175.8,
          "end": 177.69,
          "en": "So they offer for every recipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 177.69,
          "end": 180.36,
          "en": "and we return the transformed recipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 180.36,
          "end": 182.97,
          "en": "Now here my idea is to return the original recipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 182.97,
          "end": 187.29,
          "en": "but if that recipe doesn't have an ingredients array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 187.29,
          "end": 191.31,
          "en": "to set ingredients to an empty array instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 191.31,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "And for this, I will return a new object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 197.4,
          "en": "where I use the spread operator to copy all the properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 197.4,
          "end": 200.07,
          "en": "of recipe to copy all the existing data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 200.07,
          "end": 203.46,
          "en": "And then ingredients will be set equal to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 203.46,
          "end": 205.65,
          "en": "And now I'll add a turn array expression,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 205.65,
          "end": 209.28,
          "en": "where I simply check whether recipe ingredients is true ish,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 209.28,
          "end": 213.12,
          "en": "which it is if it is an array with zero or more elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 213.12,
          "end": 214.35,
          "en": "And if that is the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 214.35,
          "end": 216.96,
          "en": "then I will set ingredients equal to recipe ingredients,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 216.96,
          "end": 218.73,
          "en": "which means I will not change it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 218.73,
          "end": 220.5,
          "en": "But otherwise I'll set it to an MT array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 220.5,
          "end": 223.23,
          "en": "So if this here is kind of false, which is the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 223.23,
          "end": 225.84,
          "en": "if ingredients is undefined, if it's not set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 225.84,
          "end": 228.63,
          "en": "then I will set it to an MT array instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 228.63,
          "end": 230.97,
          "en": "And that's just a tiny improvement here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 230.97,
          "end": 234.81,
          "en": "in this observable chain, which doesn't break our app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 234.81,
          "end": 236.4,
          "en": "of course it shouldn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 236.4,
          "end": 238.86,
          "en": "We can still edit our recipe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 238.86,
          "end": 243.63,
          "en": "interact with it, save that, and everything works as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 243.63,
          "end": 245.94,
          "en": "But now we have a little bit more protection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 245.94,
          "end": 247.68,
          "en": "against unexpected errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 247.68,
          "end": 250.5,
          "en": "because now we ensure that the ingredients property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 250.5,
          "end": 254.823,
          "en": "of the loaded recipes is always set to at least an MT array.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
